indow of a neighbouring dwelling. | for that part between 4.5m – 7.5m | 1.5m to wall and balcony 1m to outermost projection | for that part exceeding 7.5m | 2m to wall and balcony 1.5m to outermost projection | Rear lane | 0.5m minimum 1m maximum for covered car parking$q$, 'VERIFIED_VERBATIM', $q$Table 6.2.3-1 (Part A, ruleId 469) and Table 6.2.3-2 (Part B, ruleId 490)$q$, NULL, $q$High density residential zone code (6.2.3)$q$, NULL, $q$https://cityplan.goldcoast.qld.gov.au/eplan/api/l/r/35/0/false/08-Sep-2026/false$q$, $q$Scheme definition 'Setback': shortest horizontal distance from the outermost projection of the building or structure to the vertical projection of the lot boundary. 'Outermost projection' excludes retractable blinds, fixed screens, rainwater fittings, ornamental attachments. Note: when acting as a QDC alternative provision, the building certifier may apply QDC/QHC measurement conventions (boundary clearance, also defined in Sch 1) - manual review.$q$, $q$gc_hdr_small_lot_front_setback$q$);
